    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="long-form-body">
            <h2>What that looks like in practice</h2>
            <p><strong>A 12-engineer M&E contractor</strong> pays £140/month on Quickler Business, with all twelve engineers covered and eight workflows included.</p>
            <p><strong>A 30-engineer construction firm</strong> pays £300/month on Quickler Scale, again flat.</p>
            <p>We deliberately avoid quoting other vendors' specific prices here because their tiers and discounts change. Check their own pages for current numbers.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="long-form-body">
            <h2>Where Quickler is not the right pick</h2>
            <p>If you need a full field service management platform — scheduling, dispatching, quoting, invoicing, asset tracking — Quickler is not the right tool. A full field service suite is the right pick when you want one platform to run the whole business. Quickler is for firms whose problem is specifically the compliance-paperwork half.</p>
            <p><a href="/pages/alternatives.html">Where Quickler fits and where it does not</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="long-form-body">
            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
            <h3>What if I grow past my tier's engineer count?</h3>
            <p>Move up a tier. The Team-to-Business jump is £40/month and covers up to twelve engineers. No per-engineer overage charges, no surprise bills.</p>
            <h3>Is there a setup fee?</h3>
            <p>No setup fee on standard tiers. For bespoke onboarding (custom workflow templates beyond the standard EICR, CP12, van check and structural set), one-off setup is quoted per project.</p>
            <h3>Is there a free trial?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Sign up at app.quickler.co/signup. The trial covers one live workflow so a real engineer can run a real check and a real PDF comes out the other end. Setup to first live workflow typically takes under a week.</p>
            <h3>What if we only need it for three months of the year?</h3>
            <p>Tiers are monthly and you can cancel at any time. Data export on cancellation is supported on request.</p>
            <h3>Do you do per-engineer pricing if we prefer it?</h3>
            <p>No. Per-firm is the deliberate model — it removes the disincentive to roll the tool out across the whole team. If you want per-user pricing, iAuditor or SimPro are the right picks; the comparison page explains where each fits.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

